          <caption>
            <p>Miliary Cutaneous Tuberculosis.&#x000a0;This&#x000a0;image of the chest and upper limbs shows polymorphic dermatosis. Some plaques exhibit exulcerated areas and crusts with erythematous-violaceous borders. The middle image is a close-up view of the patient&#x02019;s trunk exhibiting dermatosis and biopsy suture The right image is a close-up view of the patient&#x02019;s right upper limb showing the patient's dermatosis. The patient is a 71-year-old immunocompromised host. Arias Sep&#x000fa;lveda C, Hernandez Rivera KJ, Olaya Cordova M, et al. Unveiling a dermatological mystery:&#x000a0;a&#x000a0;rare case of miliary cutaneous tuberculosis in an adult patient. <italic toggle="yes">Cureus.</italic> 2024;16(9):e69854. doi: <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39435193/">10.7759/cureus.69854</ext-link>.</p>
